Tables

- expense
- payment
- payment_allocations
- settlement
- expense_invitation
- user
- user_expense

expense - This is responsible for storing a list of payments from users
payment - This is a payment submitted by a user to the expense
payment_allocations - This is a join table for users who should split a payment and the amount they owe
settlement - This is responsible for tracking the settlement of payments between users
user - This is a user of the application
user_expense - This is a join table of users to expenses
expense_invitation - This stores hashed, expiring and revocable share-link invitations to expenses

View the schemas in ./lib/schemas to see the table structure

Before using expense invitations, apply ./lib/db/migrations/0001_expense_invitations.sql to the database.
Expense creator identity is stored in expense.created_by_user_id. Apply ./lib/db/migrations/0002_expense_creator.sql before using creator-only member management. Existing expenses have no creator recorded and keep removal disabled unless creator identity can be established separately.
